hi I'm Evan Carmichael and welcome to  another edition of following the Masters  I believe that the fastest and most  effective way to grow a business is to  model the strategies of people who've  already done what you're trying to do so  today we're going to look at how a young  man went against his father's wishes to  run the family business in order to  follow his dreams in the world of sports  he went on to own one of the most  successful franchises in sports history  this is a story of New York Yankees  owner George Steinbrenner and a top  three lessons that you can learn from  his success George Steinbrenner went  from coaching college football the  statement his family's business and  finally only one of the greatest  baseball franchises in history the New  York Yankees when Steinbrenner started  college he chose English literature  which is not what his father wanted him  to do instead Henry Steinbrenner wanted  George to come back I run the family  shipping business after graduating  college George went at the US Air Force  where he would get his first taste of  the business of sports by establishing a  sports program in his spare time George  had no plans on joining the family  business are ever owning a professional  sports team after his tour in the Air  Force was complete he went on to join  the coaching staff in northwestern  university and then purdue university  but family problems would take him away  from what he loved he would get a call  from his father pleading with him to  come home and help prevent the family  business from going under he told me to  get home and get busy recall  Steinbrenner I wish you could have  stayed in coaching my father never asked  that much but when he did it was an  order after successfully saving his  family shipping company and becoming  president of the company within four  years George went against his father's  wishes and left the business to pursue  his love of sports he would go on the by  to Cleveland Piper's an American  baseball league team but the league  would fold after a few seasons George  would then set his sights higher the  next time and by the new york yankees  for 8.7 million dollars in 1973  today the New York Yankees are worth  more than 1.3 billion dollars are the  most successful professional baseball  franchise in history at the same time  making George Steinbrenner one of the  greatest sports icons in history by  refusing to bow to the pressures that  his family put on him to run the family  business Steinbrenner was able to follow  his dreams and become a sports icon to  help you become an icon in your industry  here are three action items that you can  learn for george steinbrenner auction  item number one create a culture once  you start building a team around you  you'll realize how important it is to  build a culture that supports your  company you'll want people who have  different skill sets but all have the  same value system and believe in what  you're doing as a company now when  you're hiring you need to make sure  people fit within your company culture  and don't just have the skills you're  looking for one bad hire can bring the  morale and spirit of your entire  business down so take your time and do  it right George Steinbrenner knew from  the first time he stepped into ownership  with the New York Yankees that he would  have to change the perception or culture  of the team and its fans being the best  meant that he would have to get the best  players and start winning in order to  get the fans who start coming to the  games and back in the team one of his  new policies that he implemented was a  grooming of his players by implementing  a strict grooming policy he would make  sure everyone viewed the Yankees as  professionals he wanted every player to  be poster boys to others could use them  as examples to be the best you had to  look your best this policy was not just  for the players even executives and  other employees of the Yankees had to  abide by these policies according to  Steinbrenner it's an incredible  achievement particularly when i remember  that when i bought the Yankees we had  trouble drawing 1 million to the stadium  we have the greatest fans in the world  winning was everything I don't care what  to tell you winning is the most  important thing in my life after  breathing breathing first winning next  action item number to earn by working  hard you won't find many successful  entrepreneurs he'll tell you that it was  easy to build a big business being an  entrepreneur comes with a lot of hard  work and energy it's going to be more  work than any job you've ever had but  hopefully it's also a lot more fun than  you've ever had to it all starts with  hard work if you're not willing to give  it everything you've got don't expect  anything great to happen one thing that  george steinbrenner believed in down to  his core was that a person can only be  an earner if they worked hard a hard  worker can get themselves out of a lot  of trouble and build a business that is  successful he believed that working hard  could bring along its benefits by  working hard a person can do just about  anything they want and having people  around you that work hard will also make  you even more successful Steinbrenner's  working habits reflect that value system  he worked from home from eight a.m.  until noon when he left for the office  and worked there until 7pm he would make  his last call 11pm before retiring for  the day according to Steinbrenner my  father wasn't a believer in monetary  allowances for my sisters and me so he  set us up raising chickens we sold the  eggs to our neighbors one of our  neighbors one of the fresh chicken then  we also had to kill undress the chicken  every night we had to update the books  and everything we sold and the earnings  would equally split three ways my best  and worst boss was the same man my  father he never and I mean never took I  can't for an answer he 